WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.040
Your character arrived in Yharnam, from a faraway land,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.520
Seeking a cure for some unnamed illness.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.700
You sign a contract, take blood,

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.880
And become a hunter of the dream,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.780
Tasked with ending the spreading scourge of beasts.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.080
Like many hunters before you,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.080
Your consciousness is now bound to the Hunter's Dream,

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.540
And you are able to project yourself into the waking world of Yharnam.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.400
At the end of the game, the nameless Moon Presence descends.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:30.440
This is a Great One.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.500
An elder being that beckoned to the hunters and conceived the Hunter's Dream.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.220
And you're here now, asking why?

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.280
Well, let me tell the story up until this point.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.760
It all began in the tombs below Yharnam.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.920
Once, what we now call Chalice Dungeons, contained an entire civilisation.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.740
It consisted of the Pthumerians, and the Great Ones.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.580
The Pthumerians were a humanoid race, but the Great Ones were far from it.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.980
Each Great One is bizarre, unique,

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:08.300
And trying to pin down their motivations, as a species or individually, is fairly futile.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.120
The only thing that's clear about them is this:

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.340
The Great Ones, like any other race, want to reproduce.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:17.440
But for them, it's difficult.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.420
Each Great One appears to be truly unique.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.900
And since that makes mating impossible, they impregnate their subjects instead.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.060
The Ring of Betrothal states that in the age of the Great Ones,

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:33.940
Certain Pthumerians were permitted to bear a special child.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.820
This union was a blood contract,

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.640
A first reference to the blood of the Great Ones.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.740
Most of these births failed.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.320
But some didn't.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.320
At some point, the Great Ones ascended.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:52.380
We know this, because there are multiple references to some Great Ones being left behind.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.620
The Great Ones moved on to the Nightmare Realm,

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.020
And the Pthumerians were left alone,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.920
Destined to watch over the physical remains of the slumbering Great Ones.

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:06.940
In time, the Pthumerian civilisation fell to the plague of beasts.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.360
Perhaps it was something in the blood.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.020
Eventually, a group of Byrgenwerth scholars stumbled upon this place,

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.680
And the events of Bloodborne were set into motion.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.000
The scholars discovered the Old Blood of the Great Ones,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.860
A miraculous substance that made their dream of evolution a reality.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.680
The School of Byrgenwerth was headed by Master Willem,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.280
An ambitious, yet cautious man,

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:34.960
Willem desired to ascend to a higher plane of existence,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.700
And believed that the knowledge of the Great Ones would lead him there.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.840
On the other hand, one of Willem's associates, Laurence,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.720
Believed that mankind could ascend through use of the Old Blood,

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.400
The blood of the Great Ones.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.300
Laurence seems headstrong and rash,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.300
Where Willem advised caution.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.000
When we inspect the skull after defeating Vicar Amelia,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.840
This is the conflict we see.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:09.380
Laurence tells Willem he will always fear the Old Blood,

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.020
Yet he goes on to found the Healing Church,

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.460
A faith built upon the miraculous Old Blood.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.140
Meanwhile, Willem remains behind, at Byrgenwerth,

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.620
And decides to pursue alternate methods to ascension.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.740
Laurence and his Church were essential to the power in Yharnam,

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.740
Perhaps they even built the place.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.720
Blood ministers doled out the miraculous healing blood to the populace,

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.800
And the city evolved to reflect that.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.900
People came from far and wide, just like you did,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.700
For the chance to be healed.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.940
The Yharnamites whose doors you knock on are quite arrogant and proud,

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:45.940
And dislike outsiders.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.520
However, after the Old Blood was introduced into the populace,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.960
People began turning into beasts.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:58.360
"You stop right there. Not an inch closer."

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.080
In response, the Church funded the Hunter's Workshop,

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.920
With Gehrman at its head.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.960
Gehrman's methods defined beast hunting.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:12.320
He abandoned the notion of armour, and dressed instead for speed, and agility.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.140
With a firearm in one hand,

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:16.360
And adaptable melee weapon in the other,

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:21.400
The forces of the workshop became the city's primary defence against the beastly threat.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.620
Perhaps the workshop was even a secret organization,

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.740
For item descriptions note that:

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.660
"They worked under the cover of night."

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.520
And the location of the workshop was certainly difficult to find.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.500
In time, the Workshop would be abandoned in favor of the Black and White Church hunters.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.480
Perhaps Gehrman's Workshop failed, in keeping the scourge a secret,

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.540
Perhaps the Church required a more intimidating approach.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:51.920
Whatever the case, the hunters were fighting for something, and it wasn't just to keep the populace safe.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.580
Turns out, the Hunter's Workshop was just one of three branches of the Church.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.760
The others were the Choir,

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.240
and Mikolash's School of Mensis.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:06.480
The Choir existed to continue the work that began at Byrgenwerth,

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.680
Namely, the pursuit of insight, by way of communion with the Great Ones.

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:15.540
The Choir's work eventually led them to an audience with Ebrietas,

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.360
A left behind Great One.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.160
The School of Mensis was, as the name implies,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.420
Devoted to research and to learning.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.700
And while items descriptions state that Mensis was allied with the Healing Church,

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:35.220
In our adventures, it becomes clear that the school is responsible for most of the problems in this world.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.260
In Bloodborne, it's difficult to point to a main antagonist,

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.760
But if I had to, I'd point to Mikolash,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:44.440
Who is the head of the School of Mensis.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:50.180
Somehow, Mikolash got his hands on the umbilical cord of a Great One.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.420
These cords are very important.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.780
For simplicity's sake, think of these umbilical cords

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:59.220
As powerful relics that enable contact with the Great Ones.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:02.760
There are three of these umbilical cords in game.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.960
And they are used by three of the main characters.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:10.220
One cord was found by Mikolash, head of the School of Mensis.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.240
One cord is held by Willem, back in Byrgenwerth.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:17.060
And another cord went to Gehrman, of the Hunter's Worshop.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.940
Mikolash used his cord to perform a great ritual.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.380
It ripped a lecture hall of Mensis into the Nightmare Realm,

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:29.060
So that they could be granted audience with a being named Mergo.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:33.160
It is believed that Mergo is the child of a Great One,

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.920
Birthed through Yharnam, the Pthumerian Queen.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.580
There is little known about his power,

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.040
His origins of his significance,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:45.080
So just know for now that Mensis wanted audience with Mergo,

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.600
But that this audience came at a great cost.

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:50.120
A note in the village reads:

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.400
"The Mensis ritual must be stopped

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.560
Lest we all become beasts."

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.640
Willem used his cord to, and I quote:

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.420
"Elevate his being and thoughts to those of a Great One

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.560
By lining his brain with eyes.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.560
In the lake below him, we come across Rom, the Vacuous Spider.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:13.840
Many descriptions in game tell us that this spider hides all manner of rituals.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:19.620
In particular though, it seems that the spider is holding back the effets of the Mensis ritual.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.780
When Rom is gone, a Blood Moon descends,

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:25.760
Blurring the line between beast and man.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.040
After this event, we find the path to Yahar'gul open,

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:36.560
So our character can go through and silence the harrowing cries of Mergo, the infant Great One.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.100
The third umbilical cord found its way into Gehrman's hands

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:47.020
After his Hunter's Workshop disbanded, Gehrman was alone and unimportant.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:53.160
His only companion was this Doll, which he appears to have crafted with love and care.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:56.540
Perhaps this Doll's creator had wished for such a friend,

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.240
Albeit, in vain.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.960
His cord reads:

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:04.460
"The Great Ones that inhabit the Nightmare are sympathetic in spirit,

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.720
And often answer when called upon."

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.080
This third cord summons the Moon Presence,

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:14.680
A Great One which beckoned the hunters and conceived the Hunter's Dream.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:20.680
Gehrman got what he wanted, a companion and a purpose, but he becomes a puppet,

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:25.620
Endlessly finding and guiding hunters through the Dream, and out into the world,

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:30.680
Assumedly under the influences and desires of the Moon Presence.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:37.340
So, to recap, Mikolash, whose character is ever ambitious to ascend and become a Great One,

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:39.800
Used his cord to establish contact.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:46.680
He sacrificed his School of Mensis, and brought the consequences of that contact upon the world.

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:53.520
Willem, ever cautious, used his cord and Rom to mask the effects of that ritual.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:59.060
And Gehrman, lonely and lacking purpose, became a puppet to another Great One,

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.900
Named the Moon Presence.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.140
He guides hunters through this Dream and out into a few select locations.

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.380
The Hunter's Dream ends, when you successfully hunt down Mergo,

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:15.440
And his Nightmare of Mensis, suggesting that Mensis was the root of the scourge of beasts,

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:21.620
And perhaps, that the Moon Presence wanted the child of another Great One dead.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:26.060
When you silence Mergo, you return to the Workshop on fire,

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:28.180
The Dream's purpose is fulfilled.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.880
You approach Gehrman, Host of this Hunter's Dream,

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.600
And he tells you that he has the power to free you.

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:38.500
If you choose this option, you are unbound from the Dream.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:43.840
You lived through the Hunt, and saw the sun rise over Yharnam.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.960
If you reject Gehrman, the Moon Presence decides it needs another host for its Dream,

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:51.720
You.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.960
You become captivated by the Moon Presence,

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.620
And pledge to watch over the Hunter's Dream.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.580
But there is a third option:

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.540
Ascension.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.220
When the conditions are right for a Great One to be born,

00:10:05.220 --> 00:10:08.920
The mother and child can be harvested for an umbilical cord.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.860
But all Great Ones lose their children,

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:15.520
And yearn for a surrogate child instead, a replacement.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:21.340
Mikolash, Willem, Gehrman, they all found umbilical cords somewhere in the past,

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.800
And used them for their own needs,

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.620
But ultimately, each of them was unsuccessful,

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.920
In the contact that they had with the Great Ones.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:33.720
However, the notes of the Byrgenwerth scholars contain this information:

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:44.340
If you consume three cords, you can resist becoming the Moon Presence's captive.

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:47.460
Instead, you hunt the Moon Presence,

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.640
And afterwards, you become an infant Great One.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:53.900
Living inside the Dream the Moon Presence conceived.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.120
You managed to ascend, as no one else before you did.

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:02.300
And you will lift humanity into its next childhood.

